{"id":"jim-morris","n":"Jim Morris","photo":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/images/headshots/bio_jim_morris.jpg","bio":"Jim Morris, a geologist in Wichita, Kansas, became a Christian in 1952. At a conference led by The Navigators in 1956, he met LeRoy Eims who challenged Jim to saturate his life with the Word of God through scripture memory. He soon began leading small groups through Moody Bible’s Memorize the Word course written by Dawson Trotman and Lorne Sanny. Jim and his wife Pauline continued a lifelong disciplemaking ministry in Wichita, multiplying disciples throughout the United States, and around the world.","queue":["19131","22543","19114","19118","19119","19112","19113","24846","19129","19111","24942","23824","17592"],"talks":{"19114":{"t":"God's Objectives for Man","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D011.mp3","lk":0},"19118":{"t":"God's Objectives: the Real Purpose of Life","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D017.mp3","lk":14},"19119":{"t":"God's Plan for Our Life","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D018.mp3","lk":0},"19112":{"t":"Life-Line Illustration: Purpose of the Christian Life","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D009.mp3","lk":0},"19113":{"t":"Objective of the Christian Life","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D010.mp3","lk":1},"24846":{"t":"Primary Tool for Disciplemaking","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Scripture Memory","Discipleship"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/J137B.mp3","lk":0},"19129":{"t":"Purpose of the Christian Life","sp":"jim-morris","tp":["Lifeline Illustration","Purpose In Life"],"u":"https://discipleshiplibrary.com/api/media/D025.